00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
The Perfect Neighbor is a 2025 American documentary film directed by Geeta Gandbhir about the killing of Ajike Owens, a shooting incident on
June 2, 2023 where a white female, Susan Louise Lorincz, fatally shot Owens, her black female neighbor, in Ocala, Florida.

7
00:42:52,500 --> 00:42:58,500
The film is told in chronological order with limited narration, mostly using pre-existing police footage such as bodycams', and follows both the lead-up to the killing, the
incident itself and its aftermath, from the neighborhood disputes eventually escalating into the killing to Lorincz's conviction for manslaughter, among other charges.

8
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
As the killing itself did, the film notably questions the systemic bias
in how Florida's stand-your-ground laws are applied.

9
00:55:07,500 --> 00:55:13,500
The film had its world premiere at the 2025 Sundance Film Festival
on January 24, where it won the Directing Award.

10
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:21,000
It had a limited theatrical release in the U.S.

11
01:07:22,500 --> 01:07:28,500
on October 10, prior to streaming globally on Netflix on October 17.

12
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
It received widespread acclaim for its production, direction and editing, and its effective
questioning of the circumstances surrounding Owens' death and similar incidents.

13
01:19:37,500 --> 01:19:43,500
At the 98th Academy Awards, it was nominated for Best Documentary.

14
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:51,000
